          "action": "changes",
          "by": "review page",
          "comment": "After 'It exposes the component's APIs, registers its roles, and monitors it.' the slide should also cover that a component can declare requirements for accessing AI services through the model-as-a-service operator or data products through the Data operator, or even manage its cost or carbon footprint through the cost and carbon management operators. It should mention that this list is not exhaustive and that any underlying common service could be offered through this standard pattern.",
          "fingerprint": "2169c4c13c9021f6"
        },
        {
          "at": "2026-10-18T21:09:54+01:00",
          "action": "reply",
          "by": "claude",
          "comment": "Done. After the APIs, roles and monitoring sentence, the narration now covers AI models through the Model-as-a-Service operator, data products through the Data operator, and cost and carbon through their operators. It then says the list isn't exhaustive and any common platform service can use the same pattern. On screen, the Cost, Carbon, Model Operator and Data Operator modules of the Canvas picture light up as each is named, the YAML gains a dependentModels line, and a 'Not exhaustive' line follows. The slide is now about 41 s (102 words).",
